WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.510
In 1898, Camillo Golgi
stained cells with silver,

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.310
and saw a strange structure inside them.

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.920
For decades, many scientists
thought it wasn't real at all:

4
00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.090
just a trick of the preparation.

5
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.830
Then, in the 1950s, electron
microscopes showed it clearly.

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.450
It was real.

7
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.490
So if you can enlarge an
image as much as you like,

8
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.920
why do some things inside
a cell stay blurred?

9
00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.820
In this mission, you'll
compare three microscopes,

10
00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.310
and how each one makes its image.

11
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.710
Then you'll learn to read their pictures:

12
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.920
a stained cell, a flat
slice, or a 3D surface.

13
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.150
Your mission: find out why some
things inside a cell stay blurred,

14
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.200
however much you enlarge the image.
